+`start_beat.sh` additionally provides `--list-cameras` (list names, indices and
+stable paths, then exit without launching controllers) and `--select-camera`
+(interactive terminal picker before launch). All its camera-using modes support
+these choices. For a stable ordinary-webcam selection, `--camera` also accepts
+`/dev/videoN`, `/dev/v4l/by-id/...`, and `/dev/v4l/by-path/...` device paths.
+Paths are resolved to live local video nodes; the configured Gemini's full-FOV
+policy is preserved even through a path override. See
+[camera-selection examples](RIGHT_CAMERA_PLAYBACK.md#choose-the-camera-input).
+
